From 0cd50fb9d353a595e0f59daaa906cd052e583745 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Hiltner <matthew.e.hiltner@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 20:09:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] compositor: Use sampling-safe opaque regions

Opaque regions describe exact texels, but linear filtering can sample neighboring texels across their boundary. Use an inset region for linear sampling and compositor culling.

Mipmapped painting has a wider sampling footprint, so conservatively disable opaque culling whenever any stage view may select mipmaps or the paint transform cannot be classified safely.
